**2. CONTINUOUS LATTICES.** Scott develops specialization, Scott-open sets, Scott topology, monotone nets, and Proposition 2.1 in [Specialization order](Specialization/1972_Specialization_order.md); the way-below relation, Proposition 2.2, and Definition 2.3 in [Way-below relation](WayBelow/1972_WayBelow_order.md). Proposition 2.4 through Theorem 2.12, idempotent fixed points, the order-iso and specialization lemmas used in inverse limits, and the post-theorem remarks are collected in [Continuous lattice](ContinuousLattices/1972_Continuous_lattice_order.md). The same Theorem 2.12 chain is linked again below so this section’s dependency diagram can reach those notes directly. [Scott maps](ScottMaps/1972_Scott_maps.md) and Propositions 2.8–2.11, with their proof notes, treat Scott continuity, products, and retractions on continuous lattices on the way to Proposition 2.11 and Theorem 2.12.
